//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                          I M P U L S E   F L O W   C H A N N E L S
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Impulse Flow Channels
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.1 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "Impulse Flow Channels." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote
//  every line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset
//  classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the ATR-anchored flow engine and its two
//  distinct advance modes, adaptive convergence and directional stepping; the impulse displacement
//  test that decides when the regime flips and re-anchors the line at price; the hold lock that
//  suppresses immediate re-flips through choppy conditions; the reusable engine function that
//  allows the identical logic to be evaluated on a higher timeframe for alignment checking; the
//  volatility-scaled channel construction; the multi-layer gradient rendering that fades the
//  channel from its outer edge inward; the segment separation that breaks the drawing at every
//  flip; the boundary retest engine with first-touch qualification, rejection requirement and
//  cooldown; the separate structure-break engine that distinguishes a genuine breakout from a
//  bounce; the four-factor trend strength meter built from step consistency, regime maturity,
//  channel position and displacement; the momentum divergence detector that compares price pivots
//  against oscillator pivots; the live regime statistics engine that records average regime
//  duration, observed retest outcome rates and channel width against its own baseline; the trading
//  session filter and its ATR context reporting; the channel-derived risk helper that projects
//  invalidation and objective levels from the structure itself; the complete information panel;
//  and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.1, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's visual system was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading concepts used here are public and widely
//  taught: measuring volatility with Average True Range, flipping a trend state when price
//  displaces a set multiple of that volatility away from a reference, trailing a reference through
//  a trend, building a channel at a volatility-scaled distance from it, treating a rejection from
//  a boundary as a retest and a close beyond it as a break, higher-timeframe alignment, momentum
//  divergence, and trading-session volatility differences. These concepts belong to no single
//  author and are taught freely across the trading community. The Relative Strength Index used by
//  the divergence detector is J. Welles Wilder Jr.'s publicly documented oscillator, available as
//  a Pine built-in and used here only as a raw numerical input.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own dual-mode advance model, my own re-anchoring rule on flip, my own hold
//  lock, my own reusable engine structure for higher-timeframe evaluation, my own gradient
//  layering method, my own segment separation approach, my own retest qualification and cooldown
//  logic, my own breakout classification, my own four-factor strength model and its weighting, my
//  own divergence pairing logic, my own statistics engine, my own session handling, my own risk
//  projection, and my own presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other ATR trend-channel
//  tools is therefore unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind
//  with any other author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   N O T E   O N   L A G   A N D   O N   S T A T I S T I C S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This is a trend-following tool and it carries the lag that definition implies. A regime is
//  confirmed only after price has displaced a full flip multiple of ATR, which means the first
//  part of every move is always missed. That is the price of not being whipsawed by every wiggle,
//  and it is a deliberate trade-off rather than a defect. It suits swing and position work far
//  better than scalping, and I would rather state that plainly than imply otherwise.
//
//  The statistics panel reports what has already happened on the history currently loaded on your
//  chart. Average regime duration, retest outcome rates and channel width baseline are observed
//  records, not projections, and they carry no guarantee about future behaviour. Small samples
//  mean nothing; treat any outcome rate with fewer than about twenty recorded tests as
//  uninformative. The risk helper projects levels derived from the channel geometry. It is a
//  structural reference, not a recommendation, and it does not size positions.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Use proper risk
//  management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Impulse Flow Channels", "IFC", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 200, max_lines_count = 100)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gEng = "=====  FLOW ENGINE  ====="
atrLen   = input.int(200, "Volatility Length (ATR)", minval = 5, maxval = 1000, group = gEng, tooltip = "The base measuring unit. Every distance in this tool is a multiple of it, which is what makes the same settings valid on every market and timeframe.")
flipMult = input.float(2.00, "Flip Displacement (x ATR)", minval = 0.2, maxval = 10, step = 0.1, group = gEng, tooltip = "How far price must close from the flow line before the regime flips. Higher means fewer, larger regimes.")
mode     = input.string("Adaptive Convergence", "Line Advance Mode", options = ["Adaptive Convergence", "Directional Stepping"], group = gEng, tooltip = "Adaptive Convergence: the line closes a fraction of the gap to price each bar, so it reflects what price did inside the regime.\nDirectional Stepping: the line advances a fixed ATR fraction in the regime direction, producing a monotone staircase.")
convRate = input.float(0.045, "Convergence Rate", minval = 0.005, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.005, group = gEng)
stepMult = input.float(0.030, "Step Size (x ATR)", minval = 0.001, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.001, group = gEng)
holdBars = input.int(8, "Hold Lock (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gEng, tooltip = "Blocks a new flip for this many bars after a flip. Raise it in choppy conditions to stop the regime flickering.")

gCh = "=====  CHANNEL  ====="
bandMult = input.float(1.60, "Channel Half-Width (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 8, step = 0.1, group = gCh)
showLine = input.bool(true, "Show Flow Line", group = gCh)
lineW    = input.int(2, "Flow Line Width", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = gCh)
showFill = input.bool(true, "Show Gradient Fill", group = gCh)
gradTop  = input.int(55, "Gradient Density - Outer Edge", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gCh)
gradBot  = input.int(97, "Gradient Density - Inner Edge", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gCh)
showEdge = input.bool(false, "Show Channel Edges", group = gCh)
splitSeg = input.bool(true, "Separate Regimes Visually", group = gCh)

gMtf = "=====  HIGHER-TIMEFRAME CONFIRMATION  ====="
mtfOn    = input.bool(true, "Enable Higher-Timeframe Check", group = gMtf, tooltip = "Runs the identical flow engine on a higher timeframe and reports whether the two agree. Trading with alignment is materially more reliable than trading against it.")
mtfTf    = input.timeframe("240", "Higher Timeframe", group = gMtf)
mtfTint  = input.bool(true, "Tint Background On Conflict", group = gMtf, tooltip = "Shades the background when the local regime disagrees with the higher timeframe, so a counter-trend flip is never silent.")
mtfGate  = input.bool(false, "Signals Only When Aligned", group = gMtf, tooltip = "Suppresses retest and breakout markers whenever the two timeframes disagree.")

gSig = "=====  RETEST AND BREAKOUT  ====="
showRetest  = input.bool(true, "Show Boundary Retests", group = gSig)
showBreak   = input.bool(true, "Show Structure Breaks", group = gSig, tooltip = "A retest is a touch that closes back inside. A break is a close beyond the boundary. They are different events and are marked differently.")
trendFilter = input.bool(false, "Continuation Only (Trend Filter)", group = gSig, tooltip = "ON shows only retests that agree with the current regime: upper rejections while bearish, lower rejections while bullish.")
retestGap   = input.int(3, "Minimum Bars Between Signals", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSig)
wickTouch   = input.bool(true, "Allow Wick Touch", group = gSig)

gStr = "=====  TREND STRENGTH METER  ====="
strOn     = input.bool(true, "Compute Strength Meter", group = gStr)
consistLen= input.int(20, "Consistency Window (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = gStr, tooltip = "How many recent bars are examined to see whether the flow line has been advancing in one direction.")
matureBars= input.int(40, "Maturity Reference (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 500, group = gStr, tooltip = "A regime is considered fully mature once it has lasted this many bars.")
wConsist  = input.float(0.35, "Weight - Consistency", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gStr)
wMature   = input.float(0.20, "Weight - Maturity",    minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gStr)
wPosition = input.float(0.25, "Weight - Channel Position", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gStr)
wDisplace = input.float(0.20, "Weight - Displacement", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gStr)

gDiv = "=====  MOMENTUM DIVERGENCE  ====="
divOn    = input.bool(true, "Detect Divergence", group = gDiv)
divRsi   = input.int(14, "Oscillator Length", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gDiv)
divLeft  = input.int(5, "Pivot Left",  minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = gDiv, inline = "d")
divRight = input.int(5, "Pivot Right", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = gDiv, inline = "d")
divShow  = input.bool(true, "Mark Divergence On Chart", group = gDiv)

gStat = "=====  HISTORICAL STATISTICS  ====="
statOn    = input.bool(true, "Track Statistics", group = gStat, tooltip = "Observed record of what has already happened on the loaded history. Not a projection.")
outcomeATR= input.float(0.80, "Bounce Confirmed At (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, group = gStat, tooltip = "How far price must travel back toward the channel mid before a retest counts as a successful bounce.")
outcomeMax= input.int(20, "Outcome Window (bars)", minval = 3, maxval = 200, group = gStat, tooltip = "If neither a bounce nor a break occurs within this many bars, the test is discarded rather than counted.")
widthWin  = input.int(500, "Width Baseline Window", minval = 50, maxval = 3000, group = gStat)

gSess = "=====  SESSION FILTER  ====="
sessOn   = input.bool(false, "Enable Session Filter", group = gSess, tooltip = "When enabled, signals are only marked inside the selected sessions. The panel always reports the active session regardless.")
sessTz   = input.string("UTC", "Session Timezone", group = gSess)
sessAsia = input.session("0000-0800", "Asian Session",   group = gSess)
sessLond = input.session("0700-1600", "London Session",  group = gSess)
sessNy   = input.session("1200-2100", "New York Session", group = gSess)
useAsia  = input.bool(false, "Asia",   group = gSess, inline = "s")
useLond  = input.bool(true,  "London", group = gSess, inline = "s")
useNy    = input.bool(true,  "New York", group = gSess, inline = "s")

gRisk = "=====  RISK HELPER  ====="
riskOn   = input.bool(true, "Show Risk Levels On Latest Signal", group = gRisk, tooltip = "Projects invalidation and objective levels from the channel geometry itself. A structural reference, not a recommendation.")
slBuf    = input.float(0.35, "Invalidation Buffer (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gRisk)
tpMode   = input.string("Channel Mid", "Objective", options = ["Channel Mid", "Opposite Boundary", "Risk Multiple"], group = gRisk)
tpRR     = input.float(2.0, "Risk Multiple", minval = 0.5, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gRisk)
riskExt  = input.int(25, "Level Extension (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = gRisk)
riskLbls = input.bool(false, "Show Level Labels", group = gRisk, tooltip = "OFF draws the entry, invalidation and objective as clean lines only. ON adds a text label with the price and the risk multiple.")

gInfo = "=====  INFORMATION PANEL  ====="
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show Panel", group = gInfo)
tablePos  = input.string("Top Right", "Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gInfo)
showStats = input.bool(true, "Show Statistics Section", group = gInfo)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colUp    = input.color(#26c281, "Bullish Regime", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colDn    = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish Regime", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colBrk   = input.color(#ffa726, "Structure Break", group = gSty, inline = "b")
colDiv   = input.color(#b388ff, "Divergence",      group = gSty, inline = "b")
colTblBg = input.color(#0b1020, "Panel Background", group = gSty, inline = "c")
colTblTx = input.color(#d1d4dc, "Panel Text",       group = gSty, inline = "c")
colAcc   = input.color(#f0b90b, "Accent", group = gSty)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  F L O W   E N G I N E
//  Written as a reusable function so the identical logic can be evaluated both on the chart
//  timeframe and, independently, on a higher timeframe for alignment checking. Every quantity is
//  a multiple of ATR; no raw price constant appears anywhere.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ifcEngine() =>
    float a = ta.atr(atrLen)
    var float f  = na
    var int   r  = 0
    var int   lk = 0
    var int   sb = 0
    bool fu = false
    bool fd = false

    if not na(a) and a > 0
        if na(f)
            f  := close
            r  := close >= open ? 1 : -1
            sb := bar_index
        else
            bool unlocked = lk <= 0
            float d = close - f
            if unlocked and d > a * flipMult and r != 1
                r  := 1
                f  := close
                lk := holdBars
                sb := bar_index
                fu := true
            else if unlocked and d < -a * flipMult and r != -1
                r  := -1
                f  := close
                lk := holdBars
                sb := bar_index
                fd := true
            else
                if mode == "Directional Stepping"
                    f := f + r * a * stepMult
                else
                    f := f + (close - f) * convRate
                lk := math.max(0, lk - 1)
    [f, r, sb, fu, fd, a, lk]

ifcRegimeOnly() =>
    [f, r, sb, fu, fd, a, lk] = ifcEngine()
    r

[flow, regime, segBar, flipUp, flipDown, atr, lockCnt] = ifcEngine()

int   htfRegime = mtfOn ? int(nz(request.security(syminfo.tickerid, mtfTf, ifcRegimeOnly(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off), 0)) : 0
bool  aligned   = not mtfOn or htfRegime == 0 or htfRegime == regime
bool  conflict  = mtfOn and htfRegime != 0 and htfRegime != regime

bool flipBar = flipUp or flipDown
bool bull    = regime == 1

float upper = flow + atr * bandMult
float lower = flow - atr * bandMult

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S E S S I O N   C O N T E X T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool inAsia = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessAsia, sessTz))
bool inLond = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessLond, sessTz))
bool inNy   = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessNy,   sessTz))

string sessName = inLond and inNy ? "London / NY Overlap" : inNy ? "New York" : inLond ? "London" : inAsia ? "Asia" : "Off Session"
bool sessOk = not sessOn or (useAsia and inAsia) or (useLond and inLond) or (useNy and inNy)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  R E N D E R I N G
//  The drawing is broken on every flip bar so each regime reads as its own block. The channel is
//  filled with eight layers whose transparency ramps from the outer edge inward.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool  cut  = splitSeg and flipBar
color regC = bull ? colUp : colDn

float dU = cut ? na : upper
float dL = cut ? na : lower
float dF = cut or not showLine ? na : flow

float span = dU - dL
float g0 = dL
float g1 = dL + span * 0.125
float g2 = dL + span * 0.250
float g3 = dL + span * 0.375
float g4 = dL + span * 0.500
float g5 = dL + span * 0.625
float g6 = dL + span * 0.750
float g7 = dL + span * 0.875
float g8 = dU

p0 = plot(g0, "g0", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p1 = plot(g1, "g1", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p2 = plot(g2, "g2", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p3 = plot(g3, "g3", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p4 = plot(g4, "g4", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p5 = plot(g5, "g5", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p6 = plot(g6, "g6", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p7 = plot(g7, "g7", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)
p8 = plot(g8, "g8", color = color.new(color.gray, 100), display = display.none)

gradStep(int layer) =>
    float t = gradBot - (gradBot - gradTop) * (layer / 7.0)
    int(math.max(0, math.min(100, math.round(t))))

fill(p7, p8, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(7)) : na, title = "Layer 8")
fill(p6, p7, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(6)) : na, title = "Layer 7")
fill(p5, p6, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(5)) : na, title = "Layer 6")
fill(p4, p5, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(4)) : na, title = "Layer 5")
fill(p3, p4, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(3)) : na, title = "Layer 4")
fill(p2, p3, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(2)) : na, title = "Layer 3")
fill(p1, p2, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(1)) : na, title = "Layer 2")
fill(p0, p1, color = showFill ? color.new(regC, gradStep(0)) : na, title = "Layer 1")

plot(showEdge ? dU : na, "Upper Boundary", color = color.new(regC, 30), linewidth = 1)
plot(showEdge ? dL : na, "Lower Boundary", color = color.new(regC, 30), linewidth = 1)
plot(dF, "Flow Line", color = regC, linewidth = lineW)

bgcolor(mtfOn and mtfTint and conflict ? color.new(colAcc, 92) : na, title = "Higher-Timeframe Conflict")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  R E T E S T   A N D   S T R U C T U R E   B R E A K
//  A retest is a touch that closes back inside the channel. A break is a close beyond the
//  boundary. They are different events and are handled separately.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int lastSigBar = -100000

float probeHi = wickTouch ? high : math.max(open, close)
float probeLo = wickTouch ? low  : math.min(open, close)

bool touchUp = probeHi >= upper
bool touchDn = probeLo <= lower

bool freshUp = touchUp and not touchUp[1]
bool freshDn = touchDn and not touchDn[1]

bool gapOk    = (bar_index - lastSigBar) > retestGap
bool gateOk   = (not mtfGate or aligned) and sessOk and not na(atr) and barstate.isconfirmed
bool allowUp  = not trendFilter or not bull
bool allowDn  = not trendFilter or bull

bool upRetest = showRetest and freshUp and close < upper and gapOk and gateOk and allowUp
bool dnRetest = showRetest and freshDn and close > lower and gapOk and gateOk and allowDn

bool upBreak  = showBreak and close > upper and not (close[1] > upper[1]) and gapOk and gateOk
bool dnBreak  = showBreak and close < lower and not (close[1] < lower[1]) and gapOk and gateOk

if upRetest or dnRetest or upBreak or dnBreak
    lastSigBar := bar_index

plotshape(upRetest, "Upper Rejection", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color = colDn,  size = size.tiny)
plotshape(dnRetest, "Lower Rejection", shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color = colUp,  size = size.tiny)
plotshape(upBreak,  "Upward Break",    shape.diamond,      location.abovebar, color = colBrk, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(dnBreak,  "Downward Break",  shape.diamond,      location.belowbar, color = colBrk, size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T R E N D   S T R E N G T H   M E T E R   (0 - 100)
//  Four factors: how consistently the flow line has advanced, how mature the regime is, where
//  price sits inside the channel, and how far price has displaced from the line.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
int   regimeBars = bar_index - segBar
float posInCh    = upper - lower > 0 ? (close - lower) / (upper - lower) : 0.5
float dispAtr    = atr > 0 ? (close - flow) / atr : 0.0
float slopeAtr   = not na(flow) and not na(flow[1]) and atr > 0 ? (flow - flow[1]) / atr * 100.0 : 0.0

float advCount = 0.0
for i = 0 to consistLen - 1
    float d = nz(flow[i]) - nz(flow[i + 1])
    if (bull and d > 0) or (not bull and d < 0)
        advCount += 1.0
float fConsist = consistLen > 0 ? advCount / consistLen : 0.0
float fMature  = math.min(regimeBars / math.max(matureBars, 1), 1.0)
float fPos     = bull ? posInCh : 1.0 - posInCh
float fDisp    = math.min(math.abs(dispAtr) / math.max(flipMult, 0.01), 1.0)

float wSum     = math.max(wConsist + wMature + wPosition + wDisplace, 0.0001)
float strength = strOn ? math.max(0.0, math.min(100.0, (fConsist * wConsist + fMature * wMature + fPos * wPosition + fDisp * wDisplace) / wSum * 100.0)) : na

string strTxt = na(strength) ? "-" : strength >= 80 ? "Very Strong" : strength >= 60 ? "Strong" : strength >= 40 ? "Developing" : strength >= 20 ? "Weak" : "Exhausted"

strBar(float v) =>
    int n = na(v) ? 0 : math.max(0, math.min(10, int(math.round(v / 10.0))))
    string s = ""
    for i = 1 to 10
        s := s + (i <= n ? "|" : ".")
    s

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  M O M E N T U M   D I V E R G E N C E
//  Price pivots are paired against oscillator pivots. A higher price high with a lower oscillator
//  high is bearish divergence; a lower price low with a higher oscillator low is bullish.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float osc = ta.rsi(close, divRsi)

float pvH = ta.pivothigh(high, divLeft, divRight)
float pvL = ta.pivotlow(low,   divLeft, divRight)

var float prevPH  = na
var float prevPHo = na
var float prevPL  = na
var float prevPLo = na

bool bearDiv = false
bool bullDiv = false

if divOn and not na(pvH)
    float oNow = nz(osc[divRight])
    if not na(prevPH) and not na(prevPHo)
        if pvH > prevPH and oNow < prevPHo
            bearDiv := true
    prevPH  := pvH
    prevPHo := oNow

if divOn and not na(pvL)
    float oNow = nz(osc[divRight])
    if not na(prevPL) and not na(prevPLo)
        if pvL < prevPL and oNow > prevPLo
            bullDiv := true
    prevPL  := pvL
    prevPLo := oNow

plotshape(divShow and bearDiv, "Bearish Divergence", shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color = colDiv, size = size.tiny, offset = -divRight)
plotshape(divShow and bullDiv, "Bullish Divergence", shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color = colDiv, size = size.tiny, offset = -divRight)

var int divCount = 0
if bearDiv or bullDiv
    divCount += 1

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H I S T O R I C A L   S T A T I S T I C S
//  Observed record of what actually happened on the loaded history. Not a projection.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int regDone   = 0
var int regBarSum = 0
var int prevSeg   = na

if barstate.isconfirmed and flipBar
    if not na(prevSeg)
        regBarSum += bar_index - prevSeg
        regDone   += 1
    prevSeg := bar_index

float avgRegime = regDone > 0 ? regBarSum / float(regDone) : na

// retest outcome tracking
var int   pendDir  = 0
var int   pendBar  = 0
var float pendRef  = na
var int   okCount  = 0
var int   badCount = 0

if statOn and barstate.isconfirmed
    if pendDir == 0
        if dnRetest
            pendDir := 1
            pendBar := bar_index
            pendRef := close
        else if upRetest
            pendDir := -1
            pendBar := bar_index
            pendRef := close
    else
        bool failed  = pendDir == 1 ? close < lower : close > upper
        float travel = pendDir == 1 ? close - pendRef : pendRef - close
        bool held    = atr > 0 and travel >= atr * outcomeATR
        if failed
            badCount += 1
            pendDir  := 0
        else if held
            okCount += 1
            pendDir := 0
        else if bar_index - pendBar > outcomeMax
            pendDir := 0

int   rtTotal = okCount + badCount
float rtRate  = rtTotal > 0 ? okCount / float(rtTotal) * 100.0 : na

// channel width against its own baseline
float chWidth  = upper - lower
float avgWidth = ta.sma(chWidth, widthWin)
float widthRel = not na(avgWidth) and avgWidth > 0 ? chWidth / avgWidth * 100.0 : na
string widthTxt = na(widthRel) ? "-" : widthRel >= 140 ? "Expanded" : widthRel >= 110 ? "Above Normal" : widthRel > 90 ? "Normal" : widthRel > 65 ? "Below Normal" : "Compressed"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  R I S K   H E L P E R
//  Levels are derived from the channel geometry itself, not from fixed distances, so they scale
//  with the instrument and the timeframe. A structural reference, not a recommendation.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var line  slLine  = na
var line  tpLine  = na
var line  enLine  = na
var label slLbl   = na
var label tpLbl   = na
var label enLbl   = na
var float lastRR  = na
var int   lastSide = 0

if riskOn and (upRetest or dnRetest) and not na(atr)
    line.delete(slLine)
    line.delete(tpLine)
    line.delete(enLine)
    label.delete(slLbl)
    label.delete(tpLbl)
    label.delete(enLbl)

    bool isLong = dnRetest
    float entry = close
    float stop  = isLong ? lower - atr * slBuf : upper + atr * slBuf
    float risk  = math.abs(entry - stop)
    float targ  = tpMode == "Opposite Boundary" ? (isLong ? upper : lower) : tpMode == "Risk Multiple" ? (isLong ? entry + risk * tpRR : entry - risk * tpRR) : flow

    lastRR   := risk > 0 ? math.abs(targ - entry) / risk : na
    lastSide := isLong ? 1 : -1
    color rc = isLong ? colUp : colDn

    enLine := line.new(bar_index, entry, bar_index + riskExt, entry, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(rc, 20), width = 2)
    slLine := line.new(bar_index, stop,  bar_index + riskExt, stop,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colDn, 25), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)
    tpLine := line.new(bar_index, targ,  bar_index + riskExt, targ,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colUp, 25), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)

    if riskLbls
        enLbl := label.new(bar_index + riskExt, entry, "ENTRY " + str.tostring(entry, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(rc, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        slLbl := label.new(bar_index + riskExt, stop,  "STOP "  + str.tostring(stop,  format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colDn, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        tpLbl := label.new(bar_index + riskExt, targ,  "TARGET " + str.tostring(targ, format.mintick) + (na(lastRR) ? "" : "   " + str.tostring(lastRR, "#.##") + "R"), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colUp, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S T A N C E   T O   B O U N D A R I E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float distUp    = upper - close
float distDn    = close - lower
float distUpPct = close != 0 ? distUp / close * 100.0 : na
float distDnPct = close != 0 ? distDn / close * 100.0 : na
float toFlip    = atr > 0 ? flipMult - math.abs(dispAtr) : na

string chPos = posInCh >= 0.85 ? "At Upper Edge" : posInCh >= 0.60 ? "Upper Half" : posInCh > 0.40 ? "Mid Channel" : posInCh > 0.15 ? "Lower Half" : "At Lower Edge"
string momTxt = math.abs(slopeAtr) < 1.0 ? "Flat" : math.abs(slopeAtr) < 3.0 ? "Steady" : math.abs(slopeAtr) < 6.0 ? "Strong" : "Very Strong"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N F O R M A T I O N   P A N E L
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table tbl = na

panelPos() =>
    tablePos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : tablePos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : tablePos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : tablePos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

if barstate.islast and showTable
    table.delete(tbl)
    int rows = showStats ? 16 : 11
    tbl := table.new(panelPos(), 2, rows, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colTblTx, 82), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colTblTx, 72))

    color bgH = color.new(colTblBg, 0)
    color bgR = color.new(colTblBg, 12)
    color dim = color.new(colTblTx, 45)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, "IMPULSE FLOW CHANNELS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 1, "REGIME", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 1, 1, 1)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 2, "Chart Timeframe", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 2, bull ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = regC, text_size = size.tiny)

    string htfTxt = not mtfOn ? "off" : htfRegime == 0 ? "building" : (htfRegime == 1 ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH") + (conflict ? "   CONFLICT" : "   aligned")
    color  htfCol = not mtfOn or htfRegime == 0 ? dim : conflict ? colAcc : (htfRegime == 1 ? colUp : colDn)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 3, "Higher Timeframe", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 3, htfTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = htfCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 4, "Regime Age", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 4, str.tostring(regimeBars) + " bars" + (lockCnt > 0 ? "   lock " + str.tostring(lockCnt) : ""), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = lockCnt > 0 ? colAcc : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 5, "Strength", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 5, na(strength) ? "off" : strBar(strength) + "  " + str.tostring(strength, "#") + "  " + strTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = na(strength) ? dim : strength >= 60 ? regC : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 6, "Momentum", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 6, momTxt + "   " + str.tostring(slopeAtr, "#.0") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 7, "POSITION", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 7, 1, 7)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 8, "In Channel", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 8, chPos + "   " + str.tostring(posInCh * 100, "#") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = posInCh >= 0.85 ? colDn : posInCh <= 0.15 ? colUp : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 9, "To Upper / Lower", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 9, str.tostring(distUp, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(distUpPct, "#.##") + "%)  |  " + str.tostring(distDn, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(distDnPct, "#.##") + "%)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 10, "To Flip / Session", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 10, (na(toFlip) ? "-" : str.tostring(math.max(toFlip, 0), "#.00") + "x ATR") + "   |   " + sessName, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = not na(toFlip) and toFlip < 0.5 ? colAcc : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    if showStats
        table.cell(tbl, 0, 11, "OBSERVED STATISTICS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 11, 1, 11)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 12, "Avg Regime Length", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 12, na(avgRegime) ? "-" : str.tostring(avgRegime, "#") + " bars   (" + str.tostring(regDone) + " regimes)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 13, "Retest Bounce Rate", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 13, na(rtRate) ? "-" : str.tostring(rtRate, "#") + "%   (" + str.tostring(rtTotal) + " tests)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = na(rtRate) ? dim : rtTotal < 20 ? dim : rtRate >= 50 ? colUp : colDn, text_size = size.tiny)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 14, "Channel Width", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 14, widthTxt + (na(widthRel) ? "" : "   " + str.tostring(widthRel, "#") + "% of normal"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 15, "Divergences / Last R", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 15, str.tostring(divCount) + "   |   " + (na(lastRR) ? "-" : str.tostring(lastRR, "#.##") + "R " + (lastSide == 1 ? "long" : "short")), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(flipUp,   "IFC - Bullish Regime Flip", "Impulse Flow Channels: the regime flipped bullish on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(flipDown, "IFC - Bearish Regime Flip", "Impulse Flow Channels: the regime flipped bearish on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(upRetest, "IFC - Upper Boundary Rejection", "Impulse Flow Channels: price was rejected from the upper channel boundary on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(dnRetest, "IFC - Lower Boundary Rejection", "Impulse Flow Channels: price was rejected from the lower channel boundary on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(upBreak,  "IFC - Upward Structure Break",   "Impulse Flow Channels: price closed above the upper channel boundary on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(dnBreak,  "IFC - Downward Structure Break", "Impulse Flow Channels: price closed below the lower channel boundary on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(bearDiv,  "IFC - Bearish Divergence", "Impulse Flow Channels: bearish momentum divergence detected on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(bullDiv,  "IFC - Bullish Divergence", "Impulse Flow Channels: bullish momentum divergence detected on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(conflict and not conflict[1], "IFC - Higher-Timeframe Conflict", "Impulse Flow Channels: the chart regime now disagrees with the higher timeframe on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(aligned and not aligned[1],   "IFC - Timeframes Aligned",        "Impulse Flow Channels: the chart regime now agrees with the higher timeframe on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(posInCh >= 0.85 and posInCh[1] < 0.85, "IFC - Price At Upper Edge", "Impulse Flow Channels: price reached the upper edge of the channel on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(posInCh <= 0.15 and posInCh[1] > 0.15, "IFC - Price At Lower Edge", "Impulse Flow Channels: price reached the lower edge of the channel on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(strOn and nz(strength) >= 80 and nz(strength[1]) < 80, "IFC - Trend Strength Very Strong", "Impulse Flow Channels: trend strength moved above 80 on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if flipUp
    alert("IFC Bullish Flip - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if flipDown
    alert("IFC Bearish Flip - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if upRetest
    alert("IFC Upper Rejection - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if dnRetest
    alert("IFC Lower Rejection - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if upBreak
    alert("IFC Upward Break - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if dnBreak
    alert("IFC Downward Break - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(regime,     "Regime (1 / -1)",       color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(htfRegime,  "HTF Regime (1 / -1)",   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(flow,       "Flow Line Value",       color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(strength,   "Trend Strength (0-100)",color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(dispAtr,    "Displacement (x ATR)",  color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(posInCh,    "Channel Position",      color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(regimeBars, "Regime Age (bars)",     color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(widthRel,   "Channel Width vs Norm", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(atr,        "ATR",                   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)